	<div class="col-sm-12 mb-4">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-sm-2">
				<div class="row">
					<div class="col-sm-12 m-1">
						<img class="img-fluid" alt="Graco" src="../images/site/logo-Graco-lrg.jpg" height="150" width="147">
					</div>
					<div class="col-sm-12 m-1">
						<img class="img-fluid" alt="spraying paint on a house with a Graco 190es" src="../images/site/airless-spray-painting.jpg" height="200" width="198">
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="col-sm-10">
				<p>
					The Graco 190ES is ideal for handymen, remodelers, general contractors, working property
					managers and smaller professional painting contractors with weekly spraying needs as it
					is a great pump for regular, weekly use but who are not spraying everyday. The 190ES can
					spray virtually all common paints, including stains, latex, primers and more.
				</p>
				<p>
					The fluid section on the 190ES is a double-stroke pump like those found in the Graco
					Contractor Series airless sprayers. This type of pump moves material on both the up and
					the down strokes, creating a more efficient sprayer. A hardened chrome and stainless steel
					piston pump is standard, and will result in better durability, long life, and corrosion
					protection for the sprayer.
				</p>
				<p>
					Both versions of the 190ES also feature a hi-boy cart with convenient fold-down handle
					for easy storage. The cart has a chrome&nbsp; frame which is easier to clean than painted
					ones, and includes a large capacity hose-wrap which will hold up to 100&#39; of airless
					spray hose.
				</p>
			</div>
